# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UnstableStonks configuration. Everything works out of the box against public
# endpoints — these vars only OVERRIDE defaults or unlock optional features.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. Client vars must be prefixed VITE_.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── RPC overrides (default to each network's public RPC) ────────────────────
# VITE_RPC_ROBINHOOD=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# VITE_RPC_STABLE=https://rpc.stable.xyz
# VITE_RPC_ARC=https://rpc.testnet.arc.network

# ── Block-explorer v2 API bases (default to each chain's Blockscout) ─────────
# Stable's public explorer (stablescan.xyz) is Etherscan-powered; the token/stat
# feeds use its Blockscout instance instead. Override if the host differs.
# VITE_EXPLORER_API_STABLE=https://blockscout.stable.xyz/api/v2
# VITE_EXPLORER_API_ARC=https://testnet.arcscan.app/api/v2

# ── DEX price indexers (GeckoTerminal network slug per chain) ────────────────
# Robinhood is wired ("robinhood"); Stable defaults to "stable". DYORswap (Stable's
# DEX) is indexed by GeckoTerminal, so pools populate the table once the slug is
# right — override here if GeckoTerminal lists Stable under a different slug.
# VITE_GT_NETWORK_STABLE=stable

# ── Swap routing + fee collection ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The 1% treasury fee (-> 0x6E53C6288Dc2C0F957Dc1F5E7d78874c3223CC96) works on any
# chain via a plain transfer. The DEX swap leg activates per chain once you set a
# router address (+ wrapped-native where not defaulted). Both Uniswap V2- and
# V3-style routers are supported:
#   VITE_ROUTER_<CHAIN>       router address (V2Router02 or SwapRouter02)
#   VITE_ROUTER_KIND_<CHAIN>  "v2" (default) | "v3"
#   VITE_QUOTER_<CHAIN>       QuoterV2 address — required when kind is v3
#   VITE_FEE_TIER_<CHAIN>     v3 fee tier, default 3000 (0.3%)
# Robinhood + Arc ship with VERIFIED Uniswap V3 addresses baked in (from Uniswap's
# official SDK) — no env needed. Robinhood buys/sells work out of the box.
# Override only if you want a different router:
# VITE_ROUTER_ROBINHOOD=0x...  VITE_ROUTER_KIND_ROBINHOOD=v3  VITE_QUOTER_ROBINHOOD=0x...  VITE_WNATIVE_ROBINHOOD=0x...
#
# Stable's Uniswap V3 addresses aren't in the SDK yet. Grab SwapRouter02 + QuoterV2
# + wrapped USDT0 from docs.stable.xyz/en/reference/dexes (or DYORswap, its V2 DEX)
# and set them here to enable Stable swaps + the 1% fee:
# VITE_ROUTER_STABLE=0x...        # Stable SwapRouter02 (v3) or DYORswap router (v2)
# VITE_ROUTER_KIND_STABLE=v3     # v3 for Uniswap, v2 for DYORswap
# VITE_QUOTER_STABLE=0x...        # QuoterV2 (v3 only)
# VITE_WNATIVE_STABLE=0x...       # wrapped USDT0 (WUSDT0)
# VITE_ROUTER_ARC=0x...
# VITE_WNATIVE_ARC=0x...

# ── Explorer API key (server-side secret, NOT VITE_) ─────────────────────────
# Used for two things:
#   1. New-launch discovery. The token list scans the DEX factory's pool-creation
#      logs; when the public RPC refuses eth_getLogs (common), it falls back to
#      Etherscan's logs module, which needs this key. This is the main reason to
#      set it.
#   2. A key-authenticated block height and gas price.
# NOT needed for network totals: per the Etherscan API docs
# (https://docs.etherscan.io/introduction) there is no free endpoint for "total
# transactions" / "total addresses" — those come from the explorer's own chart
# exports, which are key-less. Stable's totals populate either way.
# Get a key: https://etherscan.io/myapikey  → "Add" → copy the key.
# It is read ONLY on the server and never reaches the browser bundle.
#   Local dev:  put it in .env (this file, copied) and restart `bun run dev`
#   Production: add it as a deploy secret / environment variable, then redeploy
# STABLESCAN_API_KEY=YOUR_ETHERSCAN_KEY
# (ETHERSCAN_API_KEY and EXPLORER_API_KEY are accepted as aliases.)

# ── X (Twitter) social crawl (server-side secrets, NOT VITE_) ────────────────
# The bearer token is the ONLY source that can report reach/impressions — the
# key-less crawl counts posts and accounts, and honestly reports impressions as
# unknown. If X heat looks thin, this is the fix.
# Any of these names works: X_BEARER_TOKEN, TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN,
# X_API_BEARER_TOKEN, X_API_KEY, TWITTER_API_KEY.
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=
# Fallback: comma-separated Nitter instances used when no bearer token is set.
# X_NITTER_INSTANCES=https://nitter.net,https://nitter.poast.org

# ── Arc (Circle) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Arc runs on MAINNET. Set this to point the whole entry (chain id, RPC,
# explorer, label) back at Circle's public testnet:
# VITE_ARC_TESTNET=1
#
# The mainnet chain id is provisional — it could not be confirmed from Circle's
# docs, so the app calls eth_chainId on the RPC at startup and corrects itself.
# Set these only to override the defaults:
# VITE_CHAIN_ID_ARC=5042
# VITE_RPC_ARC=https://rpc.arc.network
# VITE_EXPLORER_ARC=https://arcscan.app
# VITE_EXPLORER_API_ARC=https://arcscan.app/api/v2
#
# On Arc the gas asset IS USDC: the native view has 18 decimals and the ERC-20
# view of the SAME funds has 6, so swaps route through the ERC-20 predeploy
# (Arc documents no wrapped-native token).
# VITE_USDC_ARC=0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000          # 6 decimals
# VITE_INTERMEDIARY_ARC=0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000  # swap routing asset
# VITE_INTERMEDIARY_DECIMALS_ARC=6
# VITE_EURC_ARC=0x89B50855Aa3bE2F677cD6303Cec089B5F319D72a          # extra routing hop
#
# Bridging needs NO configuration. Both rails are probed at runtime — Relay's
# /chains list and CCTP's on-chain contract code — so the route appears by
# itself on the day Arc's bridge opens. Nothing to redeploy.

# ── Brand artwork ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The header logo and favicon default to /stonkslogo.PNG (note the uppercase
# extension — static hosts are case-sensitive). Point them elsewhere with:
# VITE_BRAND_IMAGE=/your-image.png
#
# Social link cards need an ABSOLUTE image URL; crawlers don't resolve relative
# paths. Set your deployed origin and the card uses the local file:
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://unstablestonks.vercel.app
# Without it the card falls back to the IPFS-hosted copy of the mark.
#
# Chain logos live in public/ and are wired in src/config/chains.ts (logoUrl).
# DEX logos are matched by venue name in src/config/brand.ts (VENUE_LOGOS).

# ── Shared store (optional, free) — Upstash Redis over its REST API ──────────
# Without these the app behaves exactly as it does today: every visitor waits for
# the indexers on a cold load, and whitelist spots are numbered per browser.
# With them the server keeps three small things:
#   1. The last good token list per chain (15-min TTL), so a cold visitor paints
#      real rows — logos included — before any indexer answers.
#   2. ONE whitelist roster, so spot #7 is the 7th person overall.
#   3. Visit + event counters. Counters only, no addresses, no fingerprints.
#
# Setup (about two minutes, no card):
#   Vercel dashboard → your project → Storage → Create → Marketplace → Upstash →
#   Redis → pick a region near your users → Connect to project. Vercel injects
#   both vars below into every environment; redeploy once and it's live.
# Free tier: 256 MB, 500k commands/month, 10 GB transfer.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...
#
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN are read as aliases, so a project that
# still has Vercel's own KV vars works with no renaming.

# ── Free X crawlers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# X social heat needs no key. The crawl walks a chain of free, key-less search
# engines (DuckDuckGo lite + html, Bing, Mojeek, Ecosia, Marginalia, three
# SearXNG instances) and Nitter mirrors, moving to the next whenever one is
# blocked, rate-limited or empty. Nothing to configure.
#
# X_BEARER_TOKEN is OPTIONAL and only buys true reach (impressions). Note that
# recent search is NOT in X's Free tier — a Free-tier token returns 403 no
# matter how it is configured, and the panel now says so. Basic or purchased
# credits are required for that endpoint.
